<%- include('../partials/header', { title: 'Home' }) %>

<p>Campus study-group finder</p>
<h1>StudyHub</h1>
<p class="lead">
  Find your next study session. StudyHub is a JavaFX desktop application
  that helps students browse study groups by course, search course codes,
  and view meeting information.
</p>
<p>
  Create a group with its description, meeting time, location, and maximum
  number of members. You can also remove a group after confirming deletion.
</p>

<div class="actions">
  <a class="button" href="/documentation">Read the documentation</a>
  <a class="button" href="/quickstart">Get started</a>
  <a class="button" href="https://github.com/ElAkaya/Studyhub">View GitHub repository</a>
</div>

<figure>
  <img src="/images/studyhub-home.png"
       alt="StudyHub running on macOS with the CS101 Study Crew group in the main list">
  <figcaption>
    StudyHub running with an example study group, course filtering,
    search, and group actions.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<h2>What you can do</h2>
<div class="cards">
  <section class="card">
    <h3>Find a group</h3>
    <p>Browse the demonstration course catalog, filter groups by course,
       and search by course code.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="card">
    <h3>Explore meeting details</h3>
    <p>Open a separate window to read a group's description, course,
       meeting time, location, and capacity.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="card">
    <h3>Manage local groups</h3>
    <p>Create groups using a validated form and delete groups
       through a confirmation dialog.</p>
  </section>
</div>

<aside class="notice">
  <strong>About this demonstration:</strong>
  StudyHub is a single-user, local application with an example course
  catalog. Groups are kept in memory and reset when the application closes.
  Accounts, joining groups, and online collaboration are not included.
</aside>

